Z||000000||noyb||01-17-2001||05:29 PM||||Any thoughts on how difficult it would be to install a fastback rear clip on a coupe?  Degree of difficulty?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||01-17-2001||06:38 PM||||1 easy....10 difficult<P>Since I've never done it..its a 10.||||reg||3
Z||000002||Alex2004||01-17-2001||08:46 PM||||What year is it? We did the fastback on my 84 se, it was sorta easy, just time consuming. You can get it done in a day though.  You have to take the headliner down to unbolt some bolts there, remove the sail panels, and remove a bolt there.  There are some bolts under the tail lights that you have to remove, you have to remove the plastic fender deal over the wheel.  There are alot of bolts. I can scan a pic from out chilton manual of where they are at if you want. Hope that helps alittle! Oh, on the 84's You the amber turn signals don't work because of wiring  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Alex<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||doughboySE||01-17-2001||09:33 PM||||just curious why you would do that. there are so many of us that rather have the notch back why change to the fast back? not disrespecting the fast back i love them to but i love the notch as much.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex2004||01-17-2001||09:37 PM||||I was actually wanting to keep the notch back on it but see, my dad was like rushing into it in a way, and so, i really didn't get a change to say that i wanted to keep the notch.  And i think it is kinda dumb looking without the amber lights working.  But the fastback is cool too. the notchback, with the aero noise, and 17" 5 spoke wheels, with red paint is awesome, that is why i wanted to keep it notch also! LOL<BR>Alex...||||reg||4
Z||000005||noyb||01-17-2001||09:39 PM||||It's an 86GT rear clip to be installed on a 86SE coupe.  Not sure how serious I am about it, but just in case, I wanted to make sure that I wasn't venturing into the rocket science realm.  It's too spooky in there for me.  Thanks for the info.  If I proceed, I'll be in touch for assistance and moral support.  As for now, I'm off to my spelling lesson.  Haven't figured out what a "reat" clip is.  ||||reg||1
